classes depending on the interaction substrate domain each contains in addition to the F-box motif: FBXW proteins contain WD-40 domains, FBXL proteins contain leucine-rich repeats, and FBXO proteins contain either different protein-protein interaction modules or no recognizable motifs. The protein encoded by this gene belongs to the FBXO class. [provided by RefSeq, Feb 2014].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q8TF61","text":"Substrate-recognition component of a SCF (SKP1-CUL1-F-box protein) E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase complex. Required in the developing brain for neuronal migration and long-term cerebellar integrity. Regulates postnatal hippocampal development, synaptic vesicle release probability at excitatory synapses and readily releasable pool size at inhibitory synapses. Upon accumulation at the centriole, promotes disassembly of primary cilia and negatively regulates Sonic hedgehog signaling."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}